Caring for crops means repeated clicks: select a pot, choose a chore from its menu, then repeat for the next pot. Replanting adds more steps after each harvest.

Greenline automates this chain with Tend All, Auto-replant, and optional Auto-fertilize. You spend less time clicking through menus, while Stamina, seed, and fertilizer costs stay the same.

[size=5]Main features[/size]
[list]
[*][b]Pot grid.[/b] See every pot by floor, including empty pots, with crop countdowns and markers for mature crops and problems. Research crops (Overwinter No.1) show Needs Fertilizer, and their Pest or Frost shows as a stop of growth, not a threat.[/*]
[*][b]Pot details.[/b] Point at a grid cell or a pot in the game world to see crop details. Click a cell to open the pot's menu and move the camera there.[/*]
[*][b]Tend All.[/b] Queue pot chores with one click from planting level 3, using the game's Stamina costs and limits.[/*]
[*][b]Auto-replant.[/b] Enable it below the pot grid to let Tend All plant the same crop after harvest. To exclude a pot, disable its Auto-replant checkbox in the planting window or the pot's View window.[/*]
[*][b]Auto-fertilize.[/b] Enable it per pot to replant with the fertilizer that gives the largest speed bonus, a part dose included. For example, 1 Premium Organic Fertilizer in a pot of size 2 (+50%) beats 2 Basic Fertilizer (+30%). The pot card shows the dose. With no fertilizer, replanting continues without it.[/*]
[*][b]Replant help.[/b] If replanting cannot proceed, the planting window opens with the reason so you can choose what to do.[/*]
[*][b]English and Chinese.[/b][/*]
[/list]

Greenline stores each pot's last crop, Auto-replant setting, and Auto-fertilize setting in the save. The game ignores these values without Greenline, so you can still load the save after removing the mod.

[size=5]You may also like[/size]
If you like Greenline, try [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/15]Trapline[/url] for one-click trap collection and a compact trap grid.

[size=5]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*]Survival Log version 1.1.18153 or later. For game version 1.0, use Greenline 1.0.1.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx for Survival Log[/url]. Install it first.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx[/url] [i](if no other mods were installed before, start the game once so BepInEx finishes setup, then quit)[/i].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Survival Log\BepInEx\plugins\Greenline.dll[/code]
[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Uninstall[/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]Greenline.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

[size=5]Configuration[/size]
Greenline creates [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.survivallog.greenline.cfg[/font] when you first start the game with the mod installed.

[font=Courier New]EnablePatrol[/font] controls Tend All. [font=Courier New]WorldHoverCard[/font] controls the pot card in the game world. Both are enabled by default. The file also contains background opacity settings and a debug logging setting.

Edit the file while the game is closed. Changes apply at the next game start. See [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-sl/sl-greenline/blob/main/CONFIG.md]CONFIG.md[/url] for all settings, defaults, and accepted values.

